#' Galactosylation of bovine fetuin N-glycans in an enzyme reactor
#'
#' N-glycan profiles from bovine fetuin treated with an immobilised B4GalT1
#' reactor. The experiment examines galactose addition to desialylated,
#' degalactosylated fetuin over repeated injections at two flow rates. It
#' contains nine glycan and isomer features measured across 18 source
#' observations.
#'
#' @details
#' The substrate is foetal bovine serum fetuin treated with sialidase and
#' galactosidase. Four substrate-control columns are followed by two
#' observations at each of 2, 4 and 8 hours at 25 microlitres/minute, and at
#' 0, 2, 4 and 8 hours at 75 microlitres/minute. The first 25
#' microlitres/minute injection was excluded in the source study because of
#' acquisition loss and poor signal.
#'
#' Abundance is expressed as a percentage within the A2 or A3 glycan family,
#' not of the total glycome. Flow and time are recorded in colData. The
#' repeated control table is represented once; the columns do not establish
#' biological replication or pairing.
#'
#' Twelve A2/A2G1 treatment cells with duplicated, non-closing source values
#' and twelve A3 control cells with unresolved cross-table correspondence are
#' NA. Six additional zero measurements are NA. Original values and the
#' separate masks remain in metadata. Summing the available values therefore
#' need not give 100.
#'
#' Nine typed compositions retain distinct source isomer labels. Four fully
#' localized structures from Supplementary Figure S3 are encoded; ambiguous
#' antennae and unresolved isomer mappings retain diagram evidence.
#'
#' @format
#' A [glyexp::GlycomicSE] with 9 features and 18 observations. The abundance
#' assay is in percentage within the source glycan family.
#' @source
#' GlycoPOST GPST000738. Supplementary Table 1, sheets 1 and 2; composition
#' comparisons in sheets 5 and 6; Figure S3. Study:
#' \url{https://doi.org/10.3389/fmolb.2026.1932584}. Repository:
#' \url{https://glycopost.glycosmos.org/entry/GPST000738}.
#' @seealso [glyhub_data_conventions] for missing-value handling, annotations
#'   and access to original measurements and source coordinates.
#' @keywords datasets
"glyhub_GPST000738_N_B4GalT1"

